Faculty Office

746
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:21,040
Faculty Office

747
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:23,960
Tanaka-kun and Tanaka-sensei.

748
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:26,750
Stay like this and you'll drop from the advanced track.

749
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:28,300
Advanced track!?

750
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:32,220
Tanaka-kun's one of those advanced-track elites?!

751
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:36,180
What are you looking at?

752
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:38,810
Nothing!

753
00:07:42,230 --> 00:07:45,860
Remember to be courteous when entering the faculty office.

754
00:07:45,860 --> 00:07:47,270
I'm very sorry.

755
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:47,980
Tch...

756
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,340
That's a lot for you to handle alone.

757
00:08:07,290 --> 00:08:11,340
Those "friends" of yours couldn't spare their precious time to help?

758
00:08:11,340 --> 00:08:14,680
If you think it's so much, why don't you lend a hand?

759
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:16,390
No, I'll pass.

760
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,640
Kou!

761
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:21,640
What a pain. See ya.

762
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,850
You really won't help?!

763
00:08:24,690 --> 00:08:26,310
What a brat!

764
00:08:26,810 --> 00:08:28,570
Geez...

765
00:08:28,570 --> 00:08:30,690
Sorry about him.

766
00:08:32,530 --> 00:08:35,200
I'll get those for you. What class are you in?

767
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:38,280
Are you friends with Kou?

768
00:08:39,160 --> 00:08:41,000
We were in middle school.

769
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:44,830
For a little while, at least.

770
00:08:45,830 --> 00:08:46,830
That's great!

771
00:08:48,590 --> 00:08:50,050
Glad to hear it.

772
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:55,050
Why is Tanaka-sensei so happy about that?

773
00:08:55,050 --> 00:08:57,340
And seriously, he needs to fix that bed head.

774
00:08:57,340 --> 00:09:00,890
He may act all brusque, but try to get along with him.

775
00:09:00,890 --> 00:09:02,180
Don't ask the impossible!

776
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:10,270
I've really gotta stop looking for the old Tanaka-kun everywhere.

777
00:09:10,270 --> 00:09:13,110
Pretty sure Class 2's that way.

778
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:16,360
I've got some business upstairs.

779
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:19,160
Oh, sure. Thanks for the help.

780
00:09:23,410 --> 00:09:24,210
Murao.

781
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:37,840
Murao.

782
00:09:39,010 --> 00:09:43,180
I heard you're not coming to our after-finals karaoke party.

783
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:44,390
Yeah.

784
00:09:44,730 --> 00:09:47,390
You haven't gone to a single class gathering.

785
00:09:47,390 --> 00:09:49,150
Can't you show your face for once?

786
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:53,110
I don't feel like it.

787
00:09:53,110 --> 00:09:56,070
It's not like I have any attachment to the class anyway.

788
00:09:57,490 --> 00:09:58,610
But...

789
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:03,080
It's none of your business, Kominato-kun.

790
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,090
There you are, Futaba.

791
00:10:11,090 --> 00:10:12,960
Sure dragged your feet getting here.

792
00:10:15,380 --> 00:10:17,380
Those "friends" of yours...

793
00:10:17,930 --> 00:10:19,840
Check out this makeup.

794
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:20,970
What, hers?

795
00:10:20,970 --> 00:10:23,260
Yeah, here. It'd look great on you.

796
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:25,640
Nah, that's way too flashy.

797
00:10:23,430 --> 00:10:25,640
Even if they're only friends in name....

798
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:26,350
Just try it out.

799
00:10:26,350 --> 00:10:28,140
What're you looking at?

800
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:30,940
It's leagues better than being alone.

801
00:10:29,850 --> 00:10:32,310
Isn't this totally nasty?

802
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:36,030
What's that in your pocket?

803
00:10:36,030 --> 00:10:37,950
Oh, this?

804
00:10:37,950 --> 00:10:39,700
Makita-san gave it to me.

805
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:43,620
Ew, gross. What made her do that?

806
00:10:43,620 --> 00:10:45,540
I saw her eating lunch alone.

807
00:10:45,540 --> 00:10:47,750
Ha, so she's a loner!

808
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:52,080
But hey, I bet she likes being alone.

809
00:10:54,590 --> 00:10:57,340
Thanks for coming to talk with me.

810
00:10:57,880 --> 00:11:00,590
She's got nerves of steel.

811
00:11:00,590 --> 00:11:02,300
Do you really think so?

812
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:04,850
What do you mean?

813
00:11:05,310 --> 00:11:09,980
Whatever. If she ever feels lonely, she can just go hit a guy up.

814
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:15,520
Right? He'll take good care of her, so it's no problem.

815
00:11:19,030 --> 00:11:23,320
Besides, isn't acting different just for the guys kinda foul play?

816
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:26,200
If you're calling it foul play,

817
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:31,580
that means you're jealous of her because the guys think she's cute.

818
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:38,130
If that's what you want,
quit whining and be cutesy like her.

819
00:11:38,130 --> 00:11:43,550
What? I don't wanna go that far just for some attention.

820
00:11:43,550 --> 00:11:47,060
All I'm saying is that I hate girls like her.

821
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:49,390
Then just leave her alone!

822
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:53,560
You're so envious, you never stop complaining about her.

823
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:59,490
Trying to put someone down might make you feel like you're on top of the world,

824
00:12:00,990 --> 00:12:03,360
but it's the complete opposite!

825
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:10,040
I...

826
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:13,960
I messed up!

827
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:30,770
Just kidding!

828
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:37,860
If you really hate me that much,

829
00:12:37,860 --> 00:12:42,860
then it means that I've got a nice little place inside your minds.

830
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:46,990
Serves you right!

831
00:12:47,870 --> 00:12:49,790
Holy crap!

832
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:53,080
God, I feel like throwing up.

833
00:12:57,210 --> 00:12:58,210
Futaba.

834
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:03,260
Now we know what you really think about us.

835
00:13:05,930 --> 00:13:07,470
It's over.

836
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:12,140
I just didn't want to be alone.

837
00:13:12,770 --> 00:13:17,310
I spent all this time desperately striving for that one thing.

838
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:19,320
But now...

839
00:13:20,690 --> 00:13:22,690
It's all so stupid.

840
00:13:23,150 --> 00:13:24,400
Yoshioka-san!

841
00:13:26,570 --> 00:13:27,910
U-Um...

842
00:13:27,910 --> 00:13:30,780
Thank you for sticking up for me.

843
00:13:31,330 --> 00:13:33,120
Please don't thank me.

844
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:37,790
It wasn't you I was sticking up for.

845
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:41,340
I was doing it for myself.

846
00:13:43,170 --> 00:13:46,220
I'm sorry I dragged you into it.

847
00:13:48,050 --> 00:13:50,300
But it still made me happy!

848
00:14:00,190 --> 00:14:03,980
Seriously, what am I doing...

849
00:14:05,570 --> 00:14:07,820
Why did I spill all that?

850
00:14:08,700 --> 00:14:13,950
I've always kept my thoughts bottled up inside.

851
00:14:14,750 --> 00:14:17,870
It's like you're all just pretending to be friends.

852
00:14:18,620 --> 00:14:19,330
It's pointless.

853
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:28,590
Why're you all by yourself?

854
00:14:30,010 --> 00:14:32,300
What happened to those friends of yours?

855
00:14:34,350 --> 00:14:37,730
I-It's all because you couldn't keep your mouth shut.

856
00:14:37,730 --> 00:14:38,690
Huh?

857
00:14:39,310 --> 00:14:42,270
You're the one who said we were pretending to be friends!

858
00:14:44,150 --> 00:14:45,730
So it's my fault?

859
00:14:49,610 --> 00:14:50,700
No...

860
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:54,660
It's my fault.

861
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,830
I lost sight of everything but my goal,

862
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:02,380
and forgot what was really important.

863
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:07,090
Things like emotional connections and trust...

864
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:10,970
It's all my fault.

865
00:15:14,510 --> 00:15:17,310
I'm sorry for shouting at you.

866
00:15:17,310 --> 00:15:18,480
Sure.

867
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:19,810
See you!

868
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:28,490
I'm so pathetic. Messing up every step of the way.

869
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:33,700
Let's head to the arcade after school.

870
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:35,280
I haven't got any money, man.

871
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:36,330
People!

872
00:15:37,410 --> 00:15:39,000
You're still here?!

873
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,210
Bye!

874
00:15:41,870 --> 00:15:43,080
There're more over here!

875
00:15:55,640 --> 00:15:58,720
What, can't wait till later to flirt?

876
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:07,070
What?! You're hiding me, but still!

877
00:16:02,850 --> 00:16:08,690
kudarizaka fumikiri made

878
00:16:02,850 --> 00:16:08,690
Before I knew it, I had run

879
00:16:08,690 --> 00:16:13,740
atashi wa muchuu de hashitta

880
00:16:08,690 --> 00:16:13,740
all the way down to the train tracks.

881
00:16:09,070 --> 00:16:14,030
Mixed in with his cologne is a faintly nostalgic scent.

882
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:19,370
kono koi wo saegiru you ni

883
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:19,370
What I found was that the train had departed

884
00:16:19,370 --> 00:16:24,290
densha wa sugisatta

885
00:16:19,370 --> 00:16:24,290
and taken my love with it.

886
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:26,420
If you were that caught up in your goal...

887
00:16:24,290 --> 00:16:29,960
tooi hi no kioku  umi no kagayaki

888
00:16:24,290 --> 00:16:29,960
Distant memories, shining seas.

889
00:16:28,250 --> 00:16:33,880
Well, that just means you were so desperate that you lost sight of it.

890
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:32,840
kisetsu wa meguru

891
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:32,840
Seasons pass.

892
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:37,220
hikoukigumo ni me wo hosomete

893
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:37,220
Now, I squint up at the clouds.

894
00:16:37,220 --> 00:16:42,600
chiisaku yureta himawari

895
00:16:37,220 --> 00:16:42,600
A sunflower swayed in the breeze,

896
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:48,980
sayonara mo ienai mata

897
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:48,980
seeing how I couldn't even say goodbye.

898
00:16:47,650 --> 00:16:52,570
T-Tanaka-kun, I can't tell if you're actually kind or mean.

899
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:58,830
hon no suumiri no sukima de sotto kusuguru itami

900
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:58,830
We were so tantalizingly close, yet so far apart.

901
00:16:52,570 --> 00:16:54,530
Don't ask me.

902
00:16:54,530 --> 00:16:57,240
I just do what I want.

903
00:16:58,830 --> 00:17:04,330
manatsu ni kieta hanabi ga

904
00:16:58,830 --> 00:17:04,330
If only the summer fireworks

905
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:02,870
And also, stop calling me "Tanaka" already.

906
00:17:04,330 --> 00:17:10,300
namida no saki ni utsureba

907
00:17:04,330 --> 00:17:10,300
had appeared before my tears...

908
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:05,790
Later.

909
00:17:08,130 --> 00:17:11,510
I wonder if it's painful for him to be called that.

910
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:15,720
I will kitto omoidasu wa

911
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:15,720
I will definitely remember.

912
00:17:12,130 --> 00:17:17,640
But still, if I called him Mabuchi, it'd really be like the Tanaka-kun I once knew

913
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:27,480
anata ni todoke kono basho de atashi wa matteiru

914
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:27,480
Please know that I'll be here, waiting for you.

915
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:21,520
will have completely disappeared.

916
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:22,770
I don't want that.

917
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,270
Kou!

918
00:17:28,810 --> 00:17:30,770
Suddenly calling me by my first name?

919
00:17:31,150 --> 00:17:33,280
Would it be better if I added a "-kun"?

920
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:35,240
"Kou-kun" sound good?

921
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:37,700
I don't care either way.

922
00:17:37,700 --> 00:17:39,450
Do what you want.

923
00:17:40,530 --> 00:17:41,870
Scary...

924
00:17:43,750 --> 00:17:48,830
But I guess that means I'm free to call him by his first name.

925
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:53,460
He didn't say I couldn't.

926
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:01,510
Ever since then,

927
00:18:02,430 --> 00:18:04,980
I haven't been able to talk to Asumi or Chie-chan.

928
00:18:10,190 --> 00:18:11,980
Time passed...

929
00:18:13,690 --> 00:18:16,650
Closing Ceremony

930
00:18:14,110 --> 00:18:16,650
Stand. Bow.

931
00:18:16,650 --> 00:18:18,200
I'm free!

932
00:18:16,650 --> 00:18:18,610
Closing Ceremony

933
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:19,990
Finally!

934
00:18:22,530 --> 00:18:25,040
Is this really what I want?

935
00:18:26,250 --> 00:18:31,420
I mean, we probably won't even end up in the same class next year anyway...

936
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:39,640
Asumi, Chie-chan!

937
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:42,180
Yeah?

938
00:18:42,180 --> 00:18:44,680
H-Hey...

939
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:47,230
S-Sorry about what happened.

940
00:18:48,230 --> 00:18:50,690
I shouldn't have said it like I did.

941
00:18:52,060 --> 00:18:53,150
But...

942
00:18:54,360 --> 00:18:56,030
Those were my true feelings.

943
00:18:58,570 --> 00:19:04,790
I was always afraid you might hate me, so I never acted like myself,

944
00:19:05,910 --> 00:19:06,910
but that's...

945
00:19:08,710 --> 00:19:10,040
...who I am.

946
00:19:16,510 --> 00:19:18,670
I get how you feel.

947
00:19:20,090 --> 00:19:24,010
And well, if that's how you really are,

948
00:19:24,010 --> 00:19:27,140
I don't think we can be friends anymore.

949
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:31,440
I'm not saying you're a bad person or anything.

950
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:37,400
It's just... we don't go well together.

951
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:40,700
Bye-bye.

952
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:42,570
Wait, Asumi!

953
00:19:42,570 --> 00:19:44,120
Hold on!

954
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:50,540
Yoshioka-san.

955
00:19:56,420 --> 00:19:59,880
You know how when we were younger...

956
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:04,850
...our teachers told us to play nice with our friends?

957
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:09,930
Back then, I wholeheartedly believed in those words.

958
00:20:10,810 --> 00:20:11,440
But now...

959
00:20:12,060 --> 00:20:14,560
I understand there are times things don't go well.

960
00:20:16,150 --> 00:20:19,070
What the teachers never told us

961
00:20:19,070 --> 00:20:22,950
was what to do when everything failed.

962
00:20:25,410 --> 00:20:26,070
Yoshioka-san—

963
00:20:26,070 --> 00:20:29,790
There are some things that you can't change! That's obvious!

964
00:20:33,620 --> 00:20:34,750
I...

965
00:20:36,460 --> 00:20:40,210
There are so many things I want to talk with you about.

966
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:42,920
Me too!

967
00:20:45,890 --> 00:20:46,760
See you!

968
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:48,810
Yeah, bye-bye.

969
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:56,980
I'll keep on learning things I was never taught.

970
00:20:58,400 --> 00:21:03,650
Today I learned that coming to a clean decision is one kind of strength.

971
00:21:05,070 --> 00:21:09,200
I'm stronger now than I was back then.

972
00:21:14,580 --> 00:21:16,210
I wonder why...

973
00:21:16,830 --> 00:21:19,340
Why do I have this incredible urge

974
00:21:20,130 --> 00:21:22,010
to go see Kou?

975
00:21:22,590 --> 00:21:25,470
Not the Tanaka-kun I knew in middle school,

976
00:21:25,470 --> 00:21:27,010
but the Kou of today.

977
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:33,230
I want to feel the sense of bonding that we shared that moment

978
00:21:33,230 --> 00:21:35,060
one more time!

979
00:21:41,610 --> 00:21:44,030
Did he go home already?

980
00:21:45,030 --> 00:21:46,450
Who're you looking for?

981
00:21:53,450 --> 00:21:54,370
Kou!

